A||N||2||sdelgado||Installing replacement roof back on question??||||7||
Z||000000||sdelgado||08-18-2001||10:47 AM||||I just put in a roof (with the sunroof)on my 86 2m4. When I removed the old roof, I had also removed the sticky stuff?? from around the windshield.  Do I need to put that stuff back on, what is that stuff anyway?? and where can I get it?? or can I use something else instead?? OR can I just bolt the roof without it??<P>Thanks,<P>Steven.||||reg||7
Z||000001||Oreif||08-18-2001||11:31 AM||||It's called "Butyl" It seals the roof/windshield areas to prevent water from getting trapped under the roof skin. (Rust, cracking, etc) If water gets trapped under the roof, It could freeze in winter and crack the roof. You can get it at NAPA.<BR>When applying it don't go crazy. A little goes a long way.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||sdelgado||08-18-2001||11:40 AM||||thank you very much!!||||reg||12
